From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter Laux <hunterlaux@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 10:04:37 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 54/68] drm/ingenic: Add a driver for the X2600 display
 processing unit

The display controller of the Ingenic X2600 is not the LCD controller
that ingenic-drm supports: it reads framebuffers through descriptor
chains, with a four-layer composer, a rotator and a simple read channel,
and drives a parallel TFT or an LVDS interface.

Add a driver for it that uses the simple read channel: one primary plane
(XRGB8888 or RGB565) scanned out through a self-linked descriptor, so
that a page flip changes the framebuffer address in that descriptor; the
display end interrupt is the vblank. For LVDS it drives the SoC's LVDS
PHY through the generic PHY API.

The read channel only starts once the display interface is set up and a
framebuffer is in place (started earlier it hangs busy), so the CRTC and
encoder are enabled before the planes. A read channel left running by
the boot loader or a previous kernel is stopped at probe.

The register layout and programming sequence follow Ingenic's X2600 SDK
kernel; the composer and the rotator are left alone.
